WEBVTT

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.480
What?!

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.480
Strike?!

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.970
What the hell are you talking about?!

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.280
It's an emergency!

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.320
The union would complain?

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.660
Damn them!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.760
Let them do whatever they want!

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.750
We have enough people here.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.890
Right, everyone?

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.360
Right!

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.310
Wait for us, you damned boomers.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.080
We're going to attack them from
the top and the bottom.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.830
We've started our raid into the building.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.060
It'll probably take about ten minutes to reach

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.460
the Totem Pole's underground level.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.300
Roger. We're going to start too.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.400
Fire!

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.550
I'm going in first to see how things are.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.950
When I give you the signal, rush in.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:18.750
Yes, Sir!

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.820
Priss!

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.900
Wait! Priss, I'm going with you!

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.050
Above?

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.590
No, below.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.720
This building is full of electronics
equipment above this point.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.960
So normally people can't get in there.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.760
This floor is actually the top
floor of the Totem Pole.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.390
You need a guide, don't you?

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.760
Get on.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.800
No!

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.130
Nene! Nene Romanova!

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.200
Are you okay?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.170
That's a K-suit.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.450
Chief! Chief!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.470
I got it from the maintenance building.
Only one suit is movable.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.220
Don't scare me like that!

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:09.900
Duck!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.410
Damn, have they already gotten up here?!

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.060
Roland, we're going to withdraw from here!

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.220
I have no other choice!

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.670
The freight elevator ends here.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.150
Which way?

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.480
For now...

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.390
Damn!

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.680
Chief...

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.250
We're caught in between!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.150
It's all over!

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.150
Priss!

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.520
Leon, why are you here?!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.720
Priss!

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.290
We'll talk about it later!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.690
I've opened the shutter above us.
We'll evacuate through there.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:25.890
Nene!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.700
Priss, go ahead with Nene!

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.810
Okay! Nene, get on!

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.490
Even considering your age, it
looks pretty good on you, Nick.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.720
Bullshit!

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.120
Hurry up and go!

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.730
Damn you!

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.570
What the hell?!

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.410
Nick, on your back!

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:42.380
What?!

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.270
Remove it by yourself. I'm too
close to use my gun.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.230
Oh, damn!

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.460
Withdraw the K-suit, Roland!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.730
What's going on now?!

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:16.710
You tell me to withdraw, but
the suit doesn't obey me!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.300
Damn!

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.420
Now, Roland!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.220
Right!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.360
Let's withdraw from here, Nick!
We're almost out of ammo!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.160
Yeah! Now, I can finally move easily again.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.800
Withdraw now, everyone!

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.410
Thank you, Yano.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.440
Sure!

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.060
Hold on to me tight, Nene!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.090
I'm going through them!

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.110
Ouch!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.240
What the heck is this?!

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:34.650
Damn...

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.330
Nene...

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:40.730
Not yet!
Nene...

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:41.720
Not yet!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.360
Hurry up!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:50.500
Thank you.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.000
Leon-chan, thanks!
Thank you.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.100
Leon-chan, thanks!

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.650
Give it up!

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:09.950
Damn!

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:13.190
Close it!

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:27.710
Safe!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.360
Right?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.540
What?!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:10.680
Damn!

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.250
Haruma!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:13.620
Sure.
Haruma!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.280
Sure.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.560
It's not working!

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:37.010
What'll we do?! The ammo's almost gone!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.570
What? Nobody's there?!

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.870
I've just repaired the power source.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.760
I guess the power is back.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.270
The group that took the lower levels did it.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.180
I don't think it's possible to go
back the way we came.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.550
I don't think so either.

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:51.780
The only way for us is to climb up, isn't it?

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.420
This area is so cold!

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.400
Because of the cooling design,

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:07.660
liquid nitrogen is continually
circulating in that tube.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.490
Liquid nitrogen? I see.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.110
With this extremely high density
accumulation of electronics,

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.130
the cooling system must also be extreme.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.410
Actually, this monstrous collection
of electronics equipment

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:25.010
is another pillar which supports the AD Police.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:29.050
We couldn't do our work without it.

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:35.390
I wonder if those boomers are...

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.190
It's coming, it's coming! Where,
oh, where are the boomers?!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.400
Above?!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.530
Is this data real time?

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.200
It's accurate!

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:50.100
Why are they going up?

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.150
Daley, can you hear me?

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.180
Leon, where are you now?

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:59.620
In the Electronics Center Core.
We're being chased from below.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.490
What?!

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:04.250
Almost all of them are heading toward you!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:05.890
Shake them off!

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:07.290
Don't be ridiculous!

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.930
A dead end?!

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.480
I guess we can't do anything, but climb up.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.850
We're going up that way.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.420
Do something!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.490
Do something?! First of all, I'm alone here!

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.720
I don't think so.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.930
Since he said they're going up,

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.430
why don't we as well?

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.070
You're...

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:03.940
Let's go pick them up, shall we?

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:06.950
Sure...

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.060
Something's wrong, isn't it?

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.600
So it seems.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:28.600
Exactly as I thought! Those
boomers aren't chasing us.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.470
Their target is the electronics core!

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.360
Take it in closer!

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.620
I know!

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.330
What a bad pilot! Try to do better!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.930
This is not a taxi!

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.100
Sorry, Roland!

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:12.950
If they're planning to fuse with the
electronics core as Nene said...

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:15.550
This place will be filled with them.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:21.450
Haruma, how many bullets do we have left?!

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.660
What shall we do, Roland?

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.400
I have a good idea.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:30.630
Yano, how low can this cooling
system reduce the temperature?

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:34.240
Well, this cooling system...

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.210
It depends on how much electricity
you let it consume.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:40.510
It's filled with liquid nitrogen, so
you can get the temperature...

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:41.640
No way!

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:44.940
Well, that's what I'm thinking.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.120
The two of us will do this!

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.120
Me?

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.420
I have something to ask the rest of you to do!

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.860
Oh, we don't have much time left.
We have to hurry!

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.590
Look, Sylia!

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.100
Oh, my god!

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:12.510
You're in trouble, Leon! The whole
Totem Pole is being fused!

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.950
Where are you now?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.410
Very close to the roof! Where are you now?

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.050
Right above you. Are you with all the others?

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.990
Nick and Yano are still down there.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.050
What?!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.190
It's Nene and the others!

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.460
Please hurry and rescue them!

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:33.730
Anyway, we're going to pick you up now!

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:34.630
Roger!

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.100
We did it!

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.340
I think it's a little too early to cheer.

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.810
Damn!

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.580
Damn!

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.310
Hurry it up, Yano! This place won't
keep us safe any longer!

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.120
I can't do this, Roland.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:32.960
What's wrong, Yano?

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.730
I just remembered something.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:39.370
The capacity of this cooling tower
is more than 300 tons per day!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.800
So what?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.440
In order to operate this,

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:45.840
you need a first class air
conditioning engineer license!

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:53.410
Yano, that rule is not applicable
for these bastards!

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.850
Please hurry up! We can't hold them any longer!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.950
You're going to see, boomers!

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:20.940
Haven't you finished yet, Nick?!
I don't have any bullets left!

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:29.450
Now, Leon!

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.530
Nene! Priss!

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:25.560
Linna! Mackey!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:37.840
It couldn't be helped. I only
have a third class license.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:41.940
You did a good job.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.160
The AD Police is really finished now.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:53.700
Well, take care of what I've just said.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:57.570
I understand. At the next stockholders'
meeting, I will do so.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:08.410
Mason, I'm going to let you learn
that you are just one of my pawns.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.550
You are...

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.950
What's the matter?

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.020
What is it? Why don't you answer?!

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:22.950
Boomers can't ignore my orders!

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:30.670
lmpossible, Mason can't...

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:53.960
Why don't we play?

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.900
Next Episode

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.410
Sunday is my favorite day of the week.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.120
Everyone can forget about school
or work, and do what they want.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.660
We can enjoy sweet crepes from a corner shop,

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.670
hanging out in a pedestrian mall

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:14.040
and watching street performers.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:19.550
But there will be no more Sundays like that.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.010
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
